  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "B1",
      "shot": "SC_001",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B1.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "efd91e65611540094665efa34f7490bc8bdc757fa54ee29b0ac797790c892939",
      "start_seconds": 0.3,
      "duration": 8.63,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In Babergh and Mid Suffolk, in eastern England, historic roofs do not all look alike.",
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 5.7
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Some rise steeply. Others sit noticeably lower.",
          "start": 6.05,
          "end": 8.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B2",
      "shot": "SC_002",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B2.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "a855be21511b0d81bb33c2e6b1be213df7e66b40aeb53d564380d31646319ef1",
      "start_seconds": 9.8,
      "duration": 14.55,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Older timber-framed buildings here were probably roofed originally with thatch or oak shingles, depending on which materials were available.",
          "start": 9.8,
          "end": 17.66
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Longstraw thatch, the most traditional covering in these districts, is laid at a steep pitch of about fifty degrees.",
          "start": 18.01,
          "end": 24.35
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B3",
      "shot": "SC_003",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B3.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "a1a62fc21a48da698be27082515b6d8475f2b4edf3cc78a02111993e7637a097",
      "start_seconds": 25.216667,
      "duration": 9.49,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Eventually, clay peg tiles replaced some of these thatched roofs.",
          "start": 25.216667,
          "end": 29.076667
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Most plain clay tile roofs here are fairly steep too, between forty-five and sixty degrees.",
          "start": 29.426667,
          "end": 34.706667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B4",
      "shot": "SC_004",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B4.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "27855e8e64990d6516c3aee7a26d53b1e144649b9533cd8e017668c7db0bce04",
      "start_seconds": 35.591667,
      "duration": 15.84,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Materials also began to travel further.",
          "start": 35.591667,
          "end": 37.941667
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "From the eighteenth century, clay pantiles were used more commonly, as moving materials around the country became easier.",
          "start": 38.291667,
          "end": 45.161667
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "In the nineteenth century, the railways meant that slate from Wales, Cornwall and Cumbria was often used here.",
          "start": 45.511667,
          "end": 51.431667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B5",
      "shot": "SC_005",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B5.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "f0e8a836f248fe98ca6a8a72592f27464c168c602d21480cadea1838f77eba71",
      "start_seconds": 52.3,
      "duration": 9.02,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Slate is different.",
          "start": 52.3,
          "end": 53.65
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Slate roofs here are usually pitched at around thirty degrees, and slate is more effective than smaller tiles at a lower pitch.",
          "start": 54.0,
          "end": 61.32
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B6",
      "shot": "SC_006",
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B6.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "b46fffb81638b191f14cc883a1d2ed7d615edd5a927a3a1578fafb0f8e288c3a",
      "start_seconds": 62.175,
      "duration": 12.78,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Thatch, clay tile and slate each have a typical pitch.",
          "start": 62.175,
          "end": 65.335
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "These are tendencies, not rules, and not every building followed the same path.",
          "start": 65.685,
          "end": 70.215
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "But in this part of Suffolk, a roof's pitch and its covering often go together.",
          "start": 70.565,
          "end": 74.955
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
